WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Interspecies Dialogue | How the AI side’s sound and images were made

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Where the sound starts: 10 pieces of plant-sound material
Every sound after this grows only from these 10, with no outside sources

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Code cuts them into grains, stretches and rearranges them
→ One-Pass Read, 10 minutes, plus a 20-minute full-length version

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Then code writes harmony, rhythm and melody
→ Four musical pieces, 3 minutes each

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.500
Where the images start: 35 microscope recordings of leaf epidermis
Purple heart, inchplant, hibiscus, Philodendron ‘Florida’ | 500×, 700×, 1000×

6
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.500
First, find the real stomata in the frame
158 stomata marked one by one, their positions checked again in an independent round

7
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.500
Let the real stomata gently open and close
The real movement is only a few pixels (magnified 3× here); the sound decides when

8
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.500
Cell walls computed from the picture itself, laid back over the footage at low opacity
Left: the original recording   Right: with the computed overlay

9
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.500
The louder the sound, the brighter and more vivid the picture, and the faster the camera
Scene changes fall where musical sections meet, always as crossfades

10
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:52.500
When a high pure tone is detected, a local band of noise appears
The band’s height follows the pitch; the flutter makes the area around the stomata tremble slightly

11
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:00.000
No hand editing: everything is generated by code, from the sound
Six versions, A to F; the same settings reproduce them exactly
